---
import OfferLayout from '@/layouts/OfferLayout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '@/data/site';

const title = `Privacy — ${siteSettings.siteName}`;
const description =
  'Privacy information for our offer pages, including attribution parameters, checkout providers, email contact, and data requests.';
---

<OfferLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">
    <a class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline" href="/">← Back to the offers</a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-7xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">Last updated July 30, 2026.</p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg mt-12 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        These pages use Admaxxer to measure visits, campaign attribution, and checkout activity. It
        may store a first-party visitor identifier and standard campaign parameters such as UTM,
        Google, Meta, TikTok, or Microsoft click identifiers. When you begin checkout, we also
        collect the email address you submit, offer and button placement, referring page, general
        country code supplied by Cloudflare, and the Admaxxer visitor identifier. We do not store
        your IP address in the checkout lead record.
      </p>

      <h2>Email and checkout follow-up</h2>
      <p>
        We use the email submitted at checkout to prefill the secure payment form, deliver purchase
        information, provide support, measure offer performance, and send occasional messages about
        that offer—including a reminder when a checkout is left unfinished. You can unsubscribe from
        marketing messages at any time. If you contact us, we also receive the information you
        include in your message.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a valid checkout session is created, we identify the visitor to Admaxxer using the
        submitted email and record a Lead event. Successful payments are sent to Admaxxer only after
        a signed server-to-server webhook from the selected payment provider is verified, for
        revenue attribution and advertising conversion reporting. We do not send card details to
        Admaxxer.
      </p>

      <h2>Checkout providers</h2>
      <p>
        Payment and billing data is handled by the selected processor, Dodo Payments or Stripe,
        under that provider’s privacy terms. Secure card collection is provided by the processor;
        this site never receives or stores your full card details. The processor may retain a
        payment method for an upsell you explicitly accept, and Dodo may operate its configured
        abandoned-checkout recovery flow.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Checkout lead records are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database so we can attribute campaigns,
        support buyers, avoid sending irrelevant reminders, and build consented follow-up audiences.
        We keep them only as long as reasonably needed for those purposes, legal obligations, fraud
        prevention, and accounting.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what personal information we hold, request a correction, or request deletion by
        emailing <a href={`mailto:${siteSettings.supportEmail}`}>{siteSettings.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</OfferLayout>
